            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.639,
            0.05,
            0.846,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Constructions and Tilings"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.087,
            0.453,
            0.109
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "How do we find such A and B?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.113,
            0.583,
            0.151
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "From X and Y, draw arcs above and below XY, with the same radii."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.152,
            0.584,
            0.21
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The two points at which the arcs meet, above and below XY, give us A and B, respectively."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.22,
            0.426,
            0.24
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Use this to construct an eye."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.685,
            0.207,
            0.746,
            0.248
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 6,
              "bbox": [
                0.685,
                0.207,
                0.746,
                0.248
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_1_image_6.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.253,
            0.584,
            0.313
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In Fig. 6.1, join A and B with a line. Where does AB intersect XY, and what is the angle formed between them?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.318,
            0.591,
            0.357
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We observe that AB passes through the midpoint of XY, and is also perpendicular to it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.357,
            0.592,
            0.453
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A division of a line, or any geometrical object, into two identical parts is called "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "bisection",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". A line that bisects a given line and is perpendicular to it, is called the perpendicular bisector."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.686,
            0.255,
            0.748,
            0.272
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Fig. 6.1",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.606,
            0.282,
            0.851,
            0.452
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 11,
              "bbox": [
                0.606,
                0.282,
                0.851,
                0.452
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_1_image_11.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.462,
            0.592,
            0.483
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Will the line joining the two points at which"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.137,
            0.481,
            0.847,
            0.541
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "the arcs meet, above and below XY, always be the perpendicular bisector of XY, i.e., when XY is of any length, and the arcs are drawn using a radius of any length?"
            }
          ],
          "continues_prev": true
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.545,
            0.847,
            0.622
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This can be answered through congruence. Let us consider a line segment XY. Find points A and B such that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "AX = AX = BX = BX."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Draw the lines AB, AX, AY, BX and BY. Let O be the point of intersection between AB and XY."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.63,
            0.847,
            0.69
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? Which two triangles should be congruent for AB to be the perpendicular bisector of XY (that is, O is the midpoint of XY and AB is perpendicular to XY)?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.695,
            0.6,
            0.85
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If we show that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta \\mathrm { A O X } ~ \\cong ~ \\Delta \\mathrm { A O Y } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " then "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\begin{array} { r } { \\mathrm { O X } = \\mathrm { O Y } , } \\end{array}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle AOX = \\angle AOY"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " because they are corresponding parts of congruent triangles. Since "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle  AOX"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle  A O Y"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " together form a straight angle, we have "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle AOX + \\angle AOY = 180^{\\circ}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Thus, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle AOX = \\angle AOY = 90^{\\circ}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . This establishes that O is the midpoint of XY and AB is perpendicular to XY."
            }
          ]
        },
